            <ArticleTitle>Total occlusion of the left main coronary artery associated with acute myocardial infarction. A case report.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>128-32</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A 64-year-old man with total occlusion of the left main coronary artery associated with acute anterior infarction was treated successfully with combined emergency intracoronary thrombolysis and coronary bypass surgery. Postoperative angiography demonstrated patent bypass grafts with good preservation of left ventricular function.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
